<Layout title="Editorial policy" description="Our standards for useful, careful and transparent product content."><div class="wrap page-shell"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Editorial policy' }]} /><article class="prose-page"><p class="eyebrow">How we work</p><h1>Editorial policy</h1><p class="lead">Our recommendations should help people understand a choice, not hurry them into one.</p><h2>Useful, original work</h2><p>We write for readers who need practical context. Articles and guides should explain meaningful criteria, distinguish general advice from product-specific claims, and link to sources when facts require support. We do not invent research, product testing, customer stories, qualifications, reviews or popularity figures.</p><h2>Product recommendations</h2><p>When we publish a product recommendation, we aim to explain intended use, selection criteria, supported benefits and limitations. A recommendation should have a verified retailer destination and any applicable affiliate link must be created through that retailer’s permitted tools.</p><h2>Accuracy and updates</h2><p>Product details, policies and availability can change. We date reviews where relevant and correct material errors when identified. We avoid asserting current prices or availability without a reliable, permitted and maintainable source.</p><h2>Commercial relationships</h2><p>Affiliate links may earn a commission. We disclose that relationship near recommendations and on our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure page</a>. Editorial decisions are not guarantees of retailer approval, earnings or savings.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>If you notice an error or unclear claim, please contact us through the details listed on our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> once those details are configured.</p></article></div></Layout>
